    <string name="addiction_info_title">How the detector works</string>
    <string name="addiction_info_body" formatted="false">Aevum reads the same Android usage access that already powers Digital Balance — locally on your phone, no cloud.\n\n• Opens = foreground sessions of a tracked app. Snippets under 3 seconds are ignored as noise.\n• A session running past midnight counts as an open on its start day; its duration is split at midnight for daily totals.\n• The trend and all comparisons use only completed days, weeks or months. Today is shown separately and never inflates a streak or comparison.\n• Usage pressure (0–100) summarises the last 7 complete days: 40% daily time (reference 4 h), 25% opens (reference 70/day), 20% longest session (reference 60 min), 15% night share (22–6, reference 20%). It is an orientation, not a diagnosis.\n• When you add an app, Aevum tries to backfill 45 days. Android often keeps usage events for only a few days — from then on the history grows automatically.</string>
